$-- Renders ONLY the document's own header-includes, so it can be recovered.
$--
$-- --include-in-header REPLACES the header-includes template variable rather
$-- than appending to it, and this tool always passes -H for its default
$-- styles. So a document's own header-includes never reached the preamble:
$-- the build succeeded, the package was not loaded, and a command the document
$-- defined was undefined where it was used.
$--
$-- Rendering it here, in a pass that passes no -H, gets the content back. The
$-- LaTeX writer does the escaping, so nothing has to be quoted by hand.
$for(header-includes)$
$header-includes$
$endfor$
